      'Nobody sets out for a place they cannot walk to. With the ferry carrying only the well-off, a baker posted to a bakery on an island, or a family given a house there, walked to the shore and stood facing it. Workplaces and houses on an island with no bridge now go only to the well-off; everybody else is matched to buildings they can reach, and any destination across the water — a bench, a friend, a wander spot — is swapped for the nearest one on their own ground.',
