      'People talk like people. Every citizen now has a temperament — warm, blunt, a dreamer, a worrier, a joker, proud, quiet, curious, a grumbler or steady — and it colours how they answer. A conversation is composed for the two having it: an opening that knows what they are to each other (a spouse, kin, a friend, someone they have met, a stranger, a rival), a subject one of them has a real reason to raise, a reply in the listener’s own voice, and a parting that says where they are off to. People remember what happens to them — a night gone hungry, going unpaid, sleeping rough, a fight they saw, a new friend, setting up house, a child, arriving, mastering a trade, jail, sickness, a festival, a falling-out, a loss — and ask each other about it, and they remember what they last talked about with each person and pick it up next time. The card shows their temperament, what has happened to them lately, and who they last talked with and about what.',
